{{also|brust}}

==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|brust}}, from {{inh|de|goh|brust}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*brust}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*brusts}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/bʁʊst/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Brust.ogg|a=Germany}}
* {{audio|de|De-Brust2.ogg|a=Berlin}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Brust.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{hyph|de|Brust}} 
* {{rhymes|de|ʊst|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f,^e|dim=^chen}}

# [[chest]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Kugel traf ihn mitten in die '''Brust'''.|The bullet hit him right in the '''chest'''.}}
# [[breast]] {{q|of a woman}}; [[side]] of the [[chest]] {{q|of a man}}
#: {{ux|de|Schon seit der Pubertät ist meine rechte '''Brust''' größer als die linke.|Ever since puberty my right '''breast''' is bigger than the left one.}}
#: {{ux|de|Weil ich ungleichmäßig trainiert habe, ist meine rechte '''Brust''' größer als die linke.|Because I worked out unevenly, the right '''side of''' my '''chest''' is bigger than the left side.}}
# {{lb|de|figurative}} [[bosom]] {{gloss|seat of thoughts and feelings}}
#: {{ux|de|Bitterer Hass erfüllte seine '''Brust'''.|Bitter hatred pervaded his '''bosom'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* While the singular is perfectly neutral with regard to natural gender, the plural {{m|de|Brüste}} is roughly equivalent to English {{m|en||breasts}} and is now rarely used to refer to (human) males.

